        "zh": {
          "title": "美國成立航管應變小組，感恩節前預估單日逾5.2萬架次航班",
          "summary": "美國11月13日因航管通訊設備不穩而暫停全國航班起飛。白宮成立跨部門小組防範故障重演；美國聯邦航空總署預估，感恩節疏運期間最繁忙的一天是11月24日。",
          "body": [
            "美國交通部11月23日表示，白宮已成立跨部門小組，防範感恩節疏運期間再度發生航管系統故障。小組由美國聯邦航空總署（FAA）、交通部、國防部及國家情報總監辦公室派員組成。",
            "FAA表示，11月13日因既有通訊設備運作不穩，為安全起見一度暫停全國航班起飛。當時部分無線電頻率與雷達資料仍可使用，並非所有通訊和雷達都中斷。這次成立小組是預防措施，不是宣布新的全國起飛禁令。",
            "FAA預估，感恩節前後九天將有超過41.7萬架次航班，11月24日將是最忙的一天，預計超過5.2萬架次。這是預測值，不是實際飛航統計。美國交通部建議旅客出發前向航空公司確認航班，並透過FAA網站查詢即時機場狀況。"
          ]
        },
        "en": {
          "title": "U.S. forms air traffic control task force ahead of Thanksgiving flight peak",
          "summary": "The White House formed an interagency team after unstable air traffic communications prompted a nationwide ground stop on November 13. The FAA expects November 24 to be the busiest day of the Thanksgiving travel period.",
          "body": [
            "The U.S. Department of Transportation said on November 23 that the White House had assembled an interagency task force to prevent another air traffic control disruption during Thanksgiving travel. The team includes officials from the Federal Aviation Administration (FAA), the Departments of Transportation and Defense, and the Office of the Director of National Intelligence.",
            "The FAA said instability in its legacy communications equipment prompted a precautionary nationwide ground stop on November 13. Some radio frequencies and radar feeds remained available, so the incident was not a complete loss of communications or radar. The task force is a preventive measure, not a new ground stop.",
            "The FAA forecasts more than 417,000 flights over the nine-day holiday period and expects November 24 to be the busiest day, with more than 52,000 flights. The figures are forecasts, not counts of flights already operated. The Transportation Department advised travelers to check with their airline and use the FAA’s real-time airport status service."
          ]
        },
